# A fast 32nd-note pattern of claps, rims, shakers and the crowd while P1 and P2 sweep their whole range back and
# forth (what a hand does on the device; the macro v3 crash). Knobs are read per hit, so every hit is different.
tempo 140
steps 32
tail 2.0
track snare
sweep p1 0 255 0 8
sweep p2 255 0 0 8
sweep p1 255 0 8 16
sweep p2 0 255 8 16
sweep p1 0 255 16 24
sweep p2 0 255 16 24
sweep p1 255 128 24 32
sweep p2 255 0 24 32
note 0 53 0.5 127
note 0.5 61 0.5 90
note 1 67 0.5 70
note 1.5 58 0.5 110
note 2 53 0.5 127
note 2.5 61 0.5 90
note 3 67 0.5 70
note 3.5 58 0.5 110
note 4 53 0.5 127
note 4.5 61 0.5 90
note 5 67 0.5 70
note 5.5 58 0.5 110
note 6 53 0.5 127
note 6.5 61 0.5 90
note 7 67 0.5 70
note 7.5 58 0.5 110
note 8 53 0.5 127
note 8.5 61 0.5 90
note 9 67 0.5 70
note 9.5 58 0.5 110
note 10 53 0.5 127
note 10.5 61 0.5 90
note 11 67 0.5 70
note 11.5 58 0.5 110
note 12 53 0.5 127
note 12.5 61 0.5 90
note 13 67 0.5 70
note 13.5 58 0.5 110
note 14 53 0.5 127
note 14.5 61 0.5 90
note 15 67 0.5 70
note 15.5 58 0.5 110
note 16 76 0.5 127
note 16.5 61 0.5 90
note 17 68 0.5 70
note 17.5 58 0.5 110
note 18 76 0.5 127
note 18.5 61 0.5 90
note 19 68 0.5 70
note 19.5 58 0.5 110
note 20 76 0.5 127
note 20.5 61 0.5 90
note 21 68 0.5 70
note 21.5 58 0.5 110
note 22 76 0.5 127
note 22.5 61 0.5 90
note 23 68 0.5 70
note 23.5 58 0.5 110
note 24 53 0.5 127
note 25 61 0.5 90
note 26 67 0.5 70
note 27 58 0.5 110
note 28 53 0.5 127
note 29 61 0.5 90
note 30 67 0.5 70
note 31 58 0.5 110
expect sound 0 32
expect idle 60
expect peak_below -3
